    {
      "title": "Labels, Selectors and Endpoints",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 0,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Labels, Selectors and Endpoints",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Service and Labels",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==Service== = stable virtual IP + DNS name for changing Pods",
                "Pod IP changes whenever a Pod is **replaced**, so clients use the Service",
                "==Labels== = key/value tags on objects",
                "`spec.selector`: equality only, all keys must match (**AND**)"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. From Selector to Backends",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "Ready Pods",
                    "sub": "labels match; failed probe = removed",
                    "ink": "green"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "EndpointSlices",
                    "sub": "control plane",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "kube-proxy",
                    "sub": "iptables or IPVS",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "Service",
                "Deployment, RS, Job"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Match",
                  "Equality map",
                  "Equality + `matchExpressions`"
                ],
                [
                  "Operators",
                  "`app: web`",
                  "`In`, `NotIn`, `Exists`"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Example and Mistakes",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "yaml",
              "lines": [
                "selector:",
                "  app: web",
                "ports:",
                "- port: 80",
                "  targetPort: 8080"
              ],
              "note": "matches Pod labels app=web,tier=fe"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "bash",
              "lines": [
                "kubectl get pods -l app=web",
                "kubectl get endpoints web"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Selector typo or no selector = ==empty endpoints==: refused or timeouts",
                "`port` = Service port, `targetPort` = container port; swapping breaks traffic"
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "sidebox",
              "title": "Interview Point",
              "items": [
                "**How does a Service find Pods?** Selector matches Pod labels; Ready ones become endpoints",
                "**Why no endpoints?** Selector typo, no selector, or Pods not Ready",
                "**port vs targetPort?** Service port vs container port"
              ],
              "ink": "orange"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "ClusterIP Service",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 1,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "ClusterIP Service",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. What ClusterIP Is",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==Default== Service type",
                "Virtual IP, reachable ==inside the cluster only==",
                "Not bound to any interface",
                "kube-proxy rules {blue:DNAT} it to a random ready Pod",
                "Fits internal service-to-service traffic"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Each Type Builds on the Last",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Type",
                "Adds",
                "Reach"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "ClusterIP",
                  "virtual IP",
                  "internal only"
                ],
                [
                  "NodePort",
                  "port on every node",
                  "node IPs"
                ],
                [
                  "LoadBalancer",
                  "cloud LB",
                  "external"
                ]
              ],
              "highlightRow": 0
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Example",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "bash",
              "lines": [
                "kubectl expose deploy web --port=80 --target-port=8080"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "yaml",
              "lines": [
                "apiVersion: v1",
                "kind: Service",
                "metadata: {name: web}",
                "spec:",
                "  type: ClusterIP",
                "  selector: {app: web}",
                "  ports: [{port: 80, targetPort: 8080}]"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "4. Mistakes",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`ping` fails: only Service ports answer; test with `curl` from a Pod",
                "`clusterIP: None` = ==headless==: returns Pod IPs, used with StatefulSets"
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "sidebox",
              "title": "Interview Point",
              "items": [
                "**ClusterIP?** Virtual internal IP; kube-proxy implements it",
                "**Headless Service?** Returns Pod IPs; StatefulSets",
                "**Ping fails?** IP is virtual"
              ],
              "ink": "orange"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "NodePort and LoadBalancer",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 2,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "NodePort and LoadBalancer",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. How they expose a Service",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==NodePort==: same port on every node, `30000-32767` by default",
                "==LoadBalancer==: cloud creates an external LB with a public IP or DNS name",
                "It also creates a NodePort and a ClusterIP behind it"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "Client",
                    "sub": "<nodeIP>:<nodePort>",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Cloud LB",
                    "sub": "public IP",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "NodePort",
                    "sub": "30080",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "ClusterIP",
                    "ink": "green"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Pod",
                    "ink": "black"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Compare and example",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "NodePort",
                "LoadBalancer"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Address",
                  "Node IPs, you manage firewalls",
                  "One stable external address"
                ],
                [
                  "Cost",
                  "None extra",
                  "Own cloud LB per Service"
                ],
                [
                  "Fits",
                  "Dev, bare metal",
                  "Cloud"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "yaml",
              "lines": [
                "spec:",
                "  type: NodePort",
                "  ports:",
                "  - port: 80",
                "    targetPort: 8080",
                "    nodePort: 30080"
              ],
              "note": "pinned nodePort; or type: LoadBalancer"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`kubectl get svc` shows EXTERNAL-IP ==<pending>== until the cloud provides one"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Mistakes and interview points",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "EXTERNAL-IP stuck on <pending> on minikube, kind or bare metal: no cloud controller",
                "Fix: ==MetalLB== or `minikube tunnel`",
                "`externalTrafficPolicy: Local` keeps client IP, but nodes with no local Pod drop traffic"
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "**NodePort range?** `30000-32767` by default",
                "**Three types related?** Each builds on the last: ClusterIP, NodePort, LoadBalancer",
                "**Why Ingress?** One LB for many Services, not one paid LB each"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Cluster DNS",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 3,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Cluster DNS",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Service DNS Names",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==CoreDNS== runs in `kube-system`",
                "Name: `<svc>.<namespace>.svc.cluster.local`",
                "{green:Headless} Service resolves to the **Pod IPs**",
                "StatefulSet Pods: stable `pod-0.headless-svc`"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Short Names",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Pod `/etc/resolv.conf`: cluster DNS IP, search path, ==ndots:5==",
                "Search: `<ns>.svc.cluster.local`, `svc.cluster.local`, `cluster.local`",
                "Short names expand through the search path"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Name",
                "Works"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`web`",
                  "same namespace only"
                ],
                [
                  "`web.prod`",
                  "across namespaces"
                ],
                [
                  "`web.prod.svc.cluster.local`",
                  "FQDN, safest"
                ]
              ],
              "highlightRow": 2
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Test and Debug",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "bash",
              "lines": [
                "kubectl run tmp --rm -it --image=busybox -- nslookup web.prod"
              ],
              "note": "throwaway Pod runs the lookup"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Bare `web` for another namespace's Service fails",
                "Usual causes: CoreDNS down, NetworkPolicy blocking port ==53==",
                "`kubectl get pods -n kube-system -l k8s-app=kube-dns`"
              ],
              "style": "cross",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "4. Interview Point",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "**Full Service name?** `<svc>.<ns>.svc.cluster.local`",
                "**Resolve `web`?** Search path adds the Pod's namespace",
                "**DNS failing?** Check CoreDNS Pods, port 53 policy, `nslookup`"
              ],
              "style": "number"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Ingress and Ingress Controllers",
      "role": "outline",
